# Build context hygiene. Without this the local virtualenv (~500 MB) is uploaded
# to the builder on every deploy, and any .env in the directory would be baked
# into an image layer.
#
# EVERY DIRECTORY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, deliberately.
# An unanchored `storage/` matches a directory named "storage" at ANY depth under
# BuildKit, and only at the context root under some other matchers — so it
# silently removed app/providers/storage/ from the image on the build platform
# while building perfectly on the developer's machine. That surfaced as a
# ModuleNotFoundError at container start, long after the build reported success.

/.venv/
/venv/
/tests/
/storage/
/.model_cache/

/.env
/.env.*
!/.env.example

# Safe unanchored: these names are unambiguous and should never survive into an
# image no matter where they appear.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
